# Intent: the "refused" state, so a unit Home has not approved says so instead of looking offline (owner, 2026-11-13). Home accepts the websocket and closes it with code 1008 before its hello; the websocket class does not pass the close code on, so the unit counts connects that were accepted and closed before the hello. Two in a row show the approval look: the full link screen with the slash glyph, a key and "Waiting for Home to approve me" before the first face, or the corner strip, the muted palette and the cyan ring blink after it; the steady amber ring steps aside. A "ws_refused" event goes to the host log. The first hello clears it.
# Upstream: 78/xiaozhi-esp32 main/protocols/websocket_protocol.cc and .h; m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc (MIT). Applies after 112.
# Check after a flash: with this unit's Device-Id not approved in Home: "Waiting for Home to approve me" within a minute and a cyan blink; approve it in Home: the look clears at the next connect and the unit works. A Home restart alone must read as Offline, not as waiting for approval.
diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc b/firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc
index 4040e8a..1c63120 100644
--- a/firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc
+++ b/firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc
@@ -567,7 +567,8 @@ void StackChanAvatarDisplay::ApplyLink()
     LinkLook screen = LinkLook::None;
     LinkLook strip  = LinkLook::None;
     if (!boot_done_) {
-        screen = boot_look_;
+        // Home turning the unit away outranks "Connecting to Home..." (Wi-Fi setup still comes first).
+        screen = (hub_refused_ && boot_look_ != LinkLook::WifiSetup) ? LinkLook::Approval : boot_look_;
     } else if (hub_refused_) {
         strip = LinkLook::Approval;
     } else if (hub_offline_) {
diff --git a/firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/protocols/websocket_protocol.cc b/firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/protocols/websocket_protocol.cc
